  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The thermal stability of carbonates increases down the group. So, the order of thermal stability of carbonates of alkaline earth metals is\r\n$$\r\n\\mathrm{BaCO}_3>\\mathrm{CaCO}_3>\\mathrm{MgCO}_3>\\mathrm{BeCO}_3 .\r\n$$\r\nTherefore, $\\mathrm{BaCO}_3$ is thermodynamically most stable and $\\mathrm{BeCO}_3$ is least stable.",
    "image": null
  },
